{"id": "85896", "name": "בעיה מילולית – מערכת משוואות למהירות וזמן בנסיעה ברכבת (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "In a railway journey of \\(90km\\) an increase of \\(5\\) kilometers per hour in the speed decreases the time taken by \\(15\\) minutes.\n\n <p>Write a system of equations (one equation per line) to represent this situation using \\(v\\) as the speed of the train and \\(t\\) as the time.\n <br />\n [[input:asys]] [[validation:asys]]\n [[feedback:prt1]]\n\n <p>Eliminate \\(t\\) from your equations, writing a single equation only in \\(v\\) which represents this situation.\n <br />\n [[input:veqn]] [[validation:veqn]]\n [[feedback:prt2]]\n\n <p>What is the velocity?\n [[input:ansv]] [[validation:ansv]]\n [[feedback:prt3]]", "generalfeedback": "Let \\(v\\) be the speed of the train, \\(d\\) the distance travelled and \\(t\\) time.  If \\(t\\) is the time (in hours) then \\(15\\) minutes is \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) hour.\n\n <p>We need to use the equation \\(d=v\\times t\\) twice.\n\n <p>For the original journey we have\n \\[ 90 = v\\times t.\\]\n For the faster journey we have\n \\[ 90 = (v+5)(t-1/4).\\]", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ansv", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "asys", "type": "textarea", "boxsize": 25, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": false, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "veqn", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "S0:stack_eval_assignments(exdowncase(asys));\n S0:maplist(stack_eqnprepare,S0);\n res:stack_eqncompare(S0,tsys,[v,t]);\n lv:listofvars(exdowncase(asys));", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "res", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "stack_eqncompare(S0,tsys1,[v,t])", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "TIME_UNITS_FALSE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "elementp(vt,setify(lv))", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "MISSING *", "feedback": "Please use explicit multiplication <tt>v*t</tt>.  STACK thinks your <tt>vt</tt> is a single variable!  Please try again."}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "veqn", "tans": "v^2+5*v-1800=0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "EQN-SIM-TRUE", "fe